# Build & Packaging Rules

Reference blueprint: `@BLUEPRINT-DJANGO-INNO.md` (at `C:\Users\tmkau\Documents\Rock Solid Data\BLUEPRINT-DJANGO-INNO.md`)

## Build command

Run `build_installer.bat` (or `build_installer.bat freeze` for exe only). It handles `collectstatic` → cx_Freeze → Inno Setup automatically.

## Adding a new Django app

When a new Django app is added to `INSTALLED_APPS`:
1. Add `"appname"` and `"appname.migrations"` to PACKAGES in `setup_cx_freeze.py`
2. Add `"appname"` to `zip_exclude_packages` so templates/migrations/templatetags are unpacked
3. If the app has templatetags: add `"appname.templatetags"` to PACKAGES
4. If the app has management commands: add `"appname.management"`, `"appname.management.commands"`

## Adding a new pip dependency

When a new package is added to `requirements.txt`:
1. Add the package (and its key submodules) to PACKAGES in `setup_cx_freeze.py`
2. Watch for compiled C extensions (mypyc, Cython) — these often need explicit inclusion
3. Check transitive dependencies: run `pip show <pkg>` to see what it pulls in
4. Test the frozen build with `build_installer.bat test` (runs Debug exe)

## INCLUDE_FILES vs zip_exclude_packages

- **`zip_exclude_packages`** handles Django app content automatically (templates, migrations, static, templatetags, management commands) — do NOT duplicate these in INCLUDE_FILES
- **`INCLUDE_FILES`** is only for standalone resource files: VERSION, version.py, changelog.json, staticfiles/, seed.sqlite3

## Key invariants

- Version comes from `VERSION` file only — never duplicate it
- `UPGRADE_CODE` from `.upgrade_code` — never hardcode a GUID
- `launcher.py` must abort (`sys.exit(1)`) on migration failure — never start the server with a broken DB
- GUI exe has no console — `launcher.py` wraps `main()` in try/except writing to `crash.log`
- `frozen.py` STATIC_ROOT → `_INSTALL_DIR / "_internal" / "staticfiles"`
